\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311070\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312020\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/COLRFonts.cpp"], "git_node": "5049734edf25892f67f4093504528c7452f90e9b", "git_parents": ["ed07ce2d0f8dde10ca2b8a01d8d034bea2878f7f"], "node": "52d383429609e75aac08dadcb1b4ed20a5fdb3b3", "parents": ["bd1d9c73b632f892a935c6478aaa41ac59471e77"], "tags": []}], "date": 1784031288, "git_changesets": ["06e7e75f789f590bdbf0b319baa4972bbf7c892a", "ed07ce2d0f8dde10ca2b8a01d8d034bea2878f7f", "5049734edf25892f67f4093504528c7452f90e9b"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1421": {"changesets": [{"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045057 - Validate readback surface size in VideoFrame::Resource::CopyTo.  a=pascalc\n\nA compromised decoder process (RDD/Utility) can return a readback surface\nsmaller than the VideoFrame's coded/visible size. copyPlane() uses the coded\nsize to drive row copies, reading past the end of the temp surface allocated\nfrom the (attacker-controlled) readback descriptor. Validate that aRect fits\nwithin the actual readback surface before proceeding.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308749\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310334\n", "files": ["D308749-esr140.patch", "dom/media/webcodecs/VideoFrame.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/crashtests/2045057.html", "dom/media/webcodecs/crashtests/crashtests.list"], "git_node": "513da6de06e1dd50f605292c112775eb5d386c56", "git_parents": ["5049734edf25892f67f4093504528c7452f90e9b"], "node": "8f2dc6748d883f7cc61e63e66ac690f515cd6c34", "parents": ["52d383429609e75aac08dadcb1b4ed20a5fdb3b3"], "tags": []}], "date": 1784039195, "git_changesets": ["513da6de06e1dd50f605292c112775eb5d386c56"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1422": {"changesets": [{"author": "Julian Seward \u003cjseward@acm.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051015.  .  a